.TH SDL_GetTrayMenu 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetTrayMenu \- Gets a previously created tray menu.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_tray.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_TrayMenu * SDL_GetTrayMenu(SDL_Tray *tray);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
You should have called
.BR SDL_CreateTrayMenu ()
on the tray object\[char46] This function allows you to fetch it again later\[char46]
.PP
This function does the same thing as
.BR SDL_GetTraySubmenu (),
except that it takes a
.BR SDL_Tray
instead of a
.BR SDL_TrayEntry \[char46]
.PP
A menu does not need to be destroyed; it will be destroyed with the tray\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I tray
the tray entry to bind the menu to\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the newly created menu\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function should be called on the thread that created the tray\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_CreateTray (3),
.BR SDL_CreateTrayMenu (3)
